<div class="bdc-page">
  <header class="bdc-hero">
    <div class="bdc-hero-grid"></div>
    <div class="bdc-hero-inner">
      <a href="/#market-tools" class="bdc-back">← Back to market tools</a>
      <div class="bdc-kicker">
        <span class="bdc-live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Working application · Private credit
      </div>
      <h1>BDC<br><em>Intelligence</em></h1>
      <p class="bdc-hero-deck">A working research platform for finding credit deterioration, upcoming maturities, lender disagreement, and relative-value signals across flagship private-credit managers.</p>
      <p class="bdc-hero-body">I built it to make quarterly BDC filings usable: searchable companies, comparable manager marks, visible sector exposure, source-linked evidence, and a review queue that tells an analyst where to look first.</p>
      <div class="bdc-hero-actions">
        <a href="#live-demo" class="btn-gold">Use the Embedded App</a>
        <a href="https://bdc-tracker-omega.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-outline">Open Full Application ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="bdc-hero-proof" aria-label="Application capabilities">
        <span>7 managers</span>
        <span>Company dossiers</span>
        <span>Manager comparison</span>
        <span>Source-linked evidence</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="bdc-live" id="live-demo">
      <div class="bdc-section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="section-eyebrow">Live Product</p>
          <h2>Use the actual<br><em>application</em></h2>
        </div>
        <p>The deployed product runs below with its current filing-derived dataset, native navigation, interactions, and in-product reporting status.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bdc-demo-shell" data-bdc-shell>
        <div class="bdc-demo-frame-wrap">
          <div class="bdc-demo-loading">
            <span class="bdc-demo-spinner"></span>
            <div>
              <strong>Loading the live workspace</strong>
              <p>If the embed is blocked by your browser, use “Open full screen.”</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <iframe
            id="bdc-live-frame"
            data-bdc-frame
            data-src="https://bdc-tracker-omega.vercel.app/market"
            title="Live BDC Intelligence application"
            loading="lazy"
            referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
          ></iframe>
        </div>

        <div class="bdc-demo-status">
          <p><strong>Data:</strong> Current, filing-derived research. Reporting period and coverage are shown inside the application.</p>
          <a href="https://bdc-tracker-omega.vercel.app/market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open full screen ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <noscript>
        <p class="bdc-noscript">JavaScript is required for the embedded application. <a href="https://bdc-tracker-omega.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open BDC Intelligence directly.</a></p>
      </noscript>
    </section>

    <section class="bdc-capabilities">
      <div class="bdc-section-head">
        <div>
          <p class="section-eyebrow">Product Tour</p>
          <h2>From filing to<br><em>decision</em></h2>
        </div>
        <p>The product is organized around the questions an analyst actually needs to answer, rather than around raw filing tables.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bdc-capability-grid">
        <article class="bdc-capability bdc-capability-wide">
          <p class="bdc-capability-number">01</p>
          <div>
            <span>Market monitor</span>
            <h3>See what changed and what needs review</h3>
            <p>One command center surfaces credit developments, upcoming maturities, lender disagreement, sector moves, manager snapshots, and the restructuring watchlist.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bdc-mini-tape" aria-label="Q1 2026 market monitor snapshot">
            <span>Credit developments</span>
            <strong>162</strong>
            <span>Upcoming maturities</span>
            <strong>19</strong>
            <span>Exact overlaps</span>
            <strong>18</strong>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="bdc-capability">
          <p class="bdc-capability-number">02</p>
          <span>Investigate</span>
          <h3>Search companies and open evidence</h3>
          <p>Borrower dossiers connect marks, quarter-over-quarter moves, non-accrual status, maturities, review status, evidence, and direct SEC source links.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="bdc-capability">
          <p class="bdc-capability-number">03</p>
          <span>Compare</span>
          <h3>Find disagreement between lenders</h3>
          <p>Relative-value views chart cross-manager mark dispersion for overlapping borrowers and keep each manager’s reported value comparable.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="bdc-capability">
          <p class="bdc-capability-number">04</p>
          <span>Segment</span>
          <h3>Read portfolios by manager and sector</h3>
          <p>Manager and sector workspaces make portfolio scale, attributed fair value, coverage, and concentration visible without losing the underlying company detail.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="bdc-capability">
          <p class="bdc-capability-number">05</p>
          <span>Research</span>
          <h3>Turn a thesis into a review set</h3>
          <p>The CMA Research workspace maps companies to an investment theme and keeps analogy classifications next to the filing evidence used to support them.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="bdc-build">
      <div>
        <p class="section-eyebrow">What I Built</p>
        <h2>A research workflow,<br><em>not a static dashboard</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="bdc-build-copy">
        <p>The application connects a market-level command center to queues, search, company dossiers, manager comparison, relative-value charts, sector analysis, and evidence. Every workspace is navigable and usable in the embedded product above.</p>
        <div class="bdc-build-tags">
          <span>Next.js application</span>
          <span>Financial data normalization</span>
          <span>Interactive research UX</span>
          <span>Responsive interface</span>
          <span>SEC filing evidence</span>
        </div>
        <a href="https://bdc-tracker-omega.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="bdc-build-link">Open BDC Intelligence ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
